openbim.ifc 0.3.0 includes generated entity and official PSD/QTO reference
catalogs for IFC2x3 TC1, IFC4 ADD2 TC1, and IFC4X3 ADD2.

Repository-authored Pkl contracts and tooling are licensed under
AGPL-3.0-or-later. Upstream IFC catalog facts are distributed under
CC BY-ND 4.0; the package therefore declares the aggregate expression
`AGPL-3.0-or-later AND CC-BY-ND-4.0`.

Entity rows are deterministic format shifts of structural schema facts (entity
names, immediate parents, and directly declared attribute names) from compiled
`ifc-schema` artifacts at openbimrs/ifc commit
a7c4949bb941504ce874bdec13bd81d33491b5cb. They were exported with
`ifc-schema` commit a97e8f7e646407d6a4263a664631a1877dfa2986. No EXPRESS
source or specification prose is included.

PSD/QTO rows are deterministic format shifts produced by the canonical Rust
`ifc-template-catalog` exporter at openbimrs/ifc commit
f378f824a3787a11218466a8c63ecd0984d0240b. Bundled Pkl facts preserve set
kind/name/GUID/template type, applicability, member path/GUID/kind/value type,
unit type, and source-file path/SHA-256. The source XML, descriptions, and
specification prose are not included.

Sources:
- IFC2x3 TC1: https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/RELEASE/IFC2x3/TC1/HTML/
- IFC4 ADD2 TC1: https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/RELEASE/IFC4/ADD2_TC1/HTML/
- IFC4X3 ADD2: https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/RELEASE/IFC4_3/
- PSD/QTO licensing/source index: https://technical.buildingsmart.org/standards/ifc/ifc-schema-specifications/
